{% doc %}
  One card of the Featured collection grid. Shared by the section's main
  block loop, its auto-fill loop (leftover cells in the last row are filled
  by cycling the section's own cards from the start), and the Related
  products section (which passes a product directly instead of a block).

  The card root is always an element that WRAPS the link rather than being
  it: colour swatches are links themselves, and an anchor inside an anchor is
  invalid HTML that browsers unnest, which would break both clicks. So the
  link covers image + label, and the swatches sit beside it inside the card.

  @param {object} [block] - the card block (settings: product, image,
    draft_asset, label, label_tone, link)
  @param {product} [card_product] - a product rendered directly (no block):
    image, label, and link all come from it
  @param {boolean} [is_filler] - true when this card is an auto-fill repeat:
    skips shopify_attributes and hides it from assistive tech / tab order so
    screen readers and keyboards don't hit duplicate links
  @param {boolean} [show_collection] - render the product's first collection
    title under the label (11px caps, muted); only applies when the card
    resolves to a product; defaults to false
  @param {boolean} [label_below] - place the label under the image instead of
    overlaid on it. Used for auto-sourced product cards, whose photography
    can be pale or dark with no merchant-picked tone to rely on, so an
    overlaid label is not reliably legible. Curated blocks keep the overlay.
  @example
  {% render 'featured-card', block: block %}
  {% render 'featured-card', card_product: product, label_below: true %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign cp = card_product | default: block.settings.product
  assign card_image = block.settings.image
  assign card_label = block.settings.label
  assign card_url = block.settings.link
  if cp and card_label == blank
    assign card_label = cp.title
  endif
  if cp and card_url == blank
    assign card_url = cp.url
  endif
-%}

<div
  class="image-card{% if label_below %} image-card--stacked{% endif %}{% if is_filler %} image-card--filler{% endif %}"
  {% if is_filler %}
    aria-hidden="true"
  {% else %}
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  {% endif %}
>
  {%- if card_url != blank -%}
    <a
      href="{{ card_url }}"
      class="image-card__link"
      data-card-link
      {% if is_filler %}
        tabindex="-1"
      {% endif %}
    >
  {%- else -%}
    <span class="image-card__link">
  {%- endif -%}

  <span class="image-card__frame">
    {%- if card_image == blank and cp.featured_media -%}
      {{-
        cp.featured_media
        | image_url: width: 1200
        | image_tag:
          widths: '400, 700, 1000, 1200',
          sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 33vw, 100vw',
          class: 'image-card__media',
          alt: card_label,
          loading: 'lazy'
      -}}
    {%- else -%}
      {% render 'draft-image',
        image: card_image,
        draft_asset: block.settings.draft_asset,
        img_class: 'image-card__media',
        sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 33vw, 100vw',
        alt: card_label
      %}
    {%- endif -%}
  </span>

  {%- if card_label != blank -%}
    <span class="image-card__label{% if label_below %} image-card__label--below{% elsif block.settings.label_tone == 'light' %} image-card__label--light{% endif %}">
      {%- comment -%}
        Price and compare-at ride along on the stacked (product-sourced) card,
        the same pair the grid card shows and read the same way: from the SHOWN
        VARIANT, because compare-at can be set on one colour and not another.
        theme.js finds [data-card-price]/[data-card-compare] inside any card
        and swaps them together when a swatch is picked, so this inherits that
        behaviour rather than repeating it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if label_below and cp -%}
        {%- assign shown = cp.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}
        <span class="image-card__line">
          <span class="image-card__name">{{ card_label | escape | newline_to_br }}</span>
          <span class="image-card__prices">
            <span class="image-card__price" data-card-price>{{ shown.price | money }}</span>
            <s
              class="image-card__compare"
              data-card-compare
              {% unless shown.compare_at_price > shown.price %}
                hidden
              {% endunless %}
            >
              {{- shown.compare_at_price | money -}}
            </s>
          </span>
        </span>
      {%- else -%}
        {{- card_label | escape | newline_to_br -}}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The subtitle only joins the label where the label sits BELOW the
        image. Overlaid on a curated photo it would be a second line of text
        on unknown tone, and there the label is a design caption ("Petra
        Vase") rather than the product name, so a subtitle would not follow.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if label_below and cp -%}
        {% render 'product-subtitle', product: cp, class: 'image-card__subtitle' %}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if show_collection and cp -%}
        {%- capture card_category %}{% render 'product-category', product: cp %}{% endcapture -%}
        {%- if card_category != blank -%}
          <span class="image-card__collection">{{ card_category }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if card_url != blank -%}
    </a>
  {%- else -%}
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- unless is_filler -%}
    {%- if cp -%}
      {% render 'color-swatches', product: cp, context: 'card' %}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endunless -%}
</div>
